w preparation, workplace rights, health and wellbeing while in ASIP, and accessibility and EDI considerations. This course does not carry credit weight and is evaluated as Credit/No Credit. No tuition fee is associated, however an ancillary fee will be assessed. Refer to the ASIP Fees & Financial Aid website for further details. Students who enrolled in the ASIP stream of their program in Year 2 should enrol in PDC221H1.", "title": "Arts & Science Internship Program - Essential Skills for ASIP Success ", "levelOfInstruction": "undergraduate", "prerequisitesText": "PDC230H1", "corequisitesText": null, "exclusionsText": "PDC221H1 ", "recommendedPreparation": null, "note": null, "division": "Arts and Science, Faculty of", "breadthRequirements": null, "distributionRequirements": null, "publicationSections": ["ASIP"], "cmPublicationSections": [{"section": "ASIP", "subSections": null}]}, "created": "2026-04-21@23:19:55.598", "modified": null, "lastSaved": 0, "primaryTeachMethod": "LEC", "faculty": {"code": "ARTSC", "name": "Faculty of Arts and Science"}, "coSec": {"code": "", "name": null}, "department": {"code": "ASIP", "name": "Arts & Science Internship Program"}, "title": null, "maxCredit": 0.0, "minCredit": 0.0, "breadths": [], "notes": [{"name": "Course Note", "type": "COURSE", "content": ""}], "cancelInd": "N", "subscriptionTtb": false, "subscriptionOpenData": false, "tb1Active": false, "tb2Active": false, "fullyOnline": false, "primaryFull": false, "primaryWaitlistable": false}, {"id": "69dd3ea4830c3634bbb6a1f5", "name": "Arts & Science Internship Program - Professional Skill Development I", "ucName": null, "code": "PDC320H1", "sectionCode": "F", "campus": "St. George", "sessions": ["20269"], "sections": [{"name": "LEC0101", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "0101", "meetingTimes": null, "firstMeeting": null, "instructors": null, "currentEnrolment": null, "maxEnrolment": null, "subTitle": null, "cancelInd": null, "waitlistInd": null, "deliveryModes": [], "currentWaitlist": null, "enrolmentInd": null, "tbaInd": null, "openLimitInd": null, "notes": [{"name": "Section Note", "type": "SECTION", "content": ""}], "enrolmentControls": null, "linkedMeetingSections": null}, {"name": "LEC0301", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "0301", "meetingTimes": null, "firstMeeting": null, "instructors": null, "currentEnrolment": null, "maxEnrolment": null, "subTitle": null, "cancelInd": null, "waitlistInd": null, "deliveryModes": [], "currentWaitlist": null, "enrolmentInd": null, "tbaInd": null, "openLimitInd": null, "notes": [{"name": "Section Note", "type": "SECTION", "content": ""}], "enrolmentControls": null, "linkedMeetingSections": null}, {"name": "LEC0201", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "0201", "meetingTimes": null, "firstMeeting": null, "instructors": null, "currentEnrolment": null, "maxEnrolment": null, "subTitle": null, "cancelInd": null, "waitlistInd": null, "deliveryModes": [], "currentWaitlist": null, "enrolmentInd": null, "tbaInd": null, "openLimitInd": null, "notes": [{"name": "Section Note", "type": "SECTION", "content": ""}], "enrolmentControls": null, "linkedMeetingSections": null}, {"name": "LEC5101", "type": "Lecture", "teachMethod": "LEC", "sectionNumber": "5101", "meetingTimes": null, "firstMeeting": null, "instructors": null, "currentEnrolment": null, "maxEnrolment": null, "subTitle": null, "cancelInd": null, "waitlistInd": null, "deliveryModes": [], "currentWaitlist": null, "enrolmentInd": null, "tbaInd": null, "openLimitInd": null, "notes": [{"name": "Section Note", "type": "SECTION", "content": ""}], "enrolmentControls": null, "linkedMeetingSections": null}], "duration": null, "cmCourseInfo": {"description": "This course is a mandatory component of the Arts & Science Internship Program (ASIP) for students admitted to the ASIP stream of their program for Year 2. Successful completion of this course is required for students to graduate from the ASIP stream of their program of study. The course supports students in developing transferable skills essential for success in professional environments and the evolving world of work. Delivered through an asynchronous modular format, students complete a combination of required and elective skill development modules. Required modules include: 1) Workplace Communication 2) Collaboration & Team Dynamics. Students further tailor their learning through elective modules that may include project management, critical thinking and problem solving, leadership and influence, application of workplace communication, data visualization, design thinking, universal design, and sustainable development. In addition to asynchronous skill development modules, students participate in bi-weekly synchronous lecture sections focused on recruitment cycle support. These sessions provide structured support for the job search process, including job search strategy, careers, and workplace readiness. This course does not carry credit weight and is evaluated as Credit/No Credit. No tuition fee is associated, however an ancillary fee will be assessed. Refer to the ASIP Fees & Financial Aid website for further details. Students who enrolled in the ASIP stream of their program in Year 3 should enrol in PDC330H1.", "title": "Arts & Science Internship Program - Professional Skill Development I", "levelOfInstruction": "undergraduate", "prerequisitesText": "PDC221H1 ", "corequisitesText": null, "exclusionsText": "PDC330H1", "recommendedPreparation": null, "note": null, "division": "Arts and Science, Faculty of", "breadthRequirements": null, "distributionRequirements": null, "publicationSections": ["ASIP"], "cmPublicationSections": [{"section": "ASIP", "subSections": null}]}, "created": "2026-04-21@23:19:55.598", "modified": null, "lastSaved": 0, "primaryTeachMethod": "LEC", "faculty": {"code": "ARTSC", "name": "Faculty of Arts and Science"}, "coSec": {"code": "", "name": null}, "department": {"code": "AS